  <h1>The Many Faces of On-Policy Distillation: Pitfalls, Mechanisms, and Fixes</h1>
  <p class="lead">On-policy distillation trains LLMs by having a teacher supervise the student's own generated tokens — but it can catastrophically collapse or silently fail depending on three subtle traps: prefix mismatch, biased TopK gradients, and a structural limitation of self-distillation. This post maps the design space, shows what each failure looks like, and demonstrates the fixes.</p>
